<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The wordmark: C, the app's own icon standing in for the U, then F F.

  The band here is not a drawing of the icon, it is the icon. Every path
  in the middle group is copied verbatim from ic_cuff_foreground, with one
  translate putting its 108dp canvas where this one wants it: that file
  draws the strap at x 38 and y 26, and translating by (48, -26) lands it
  at x 86 with its top on the cap line. The weave spacing, the clasp, the
  two pairs of arcs, the gradients: all of them are the icon's numbers.

  There were two drawings for a while and they drifted, which is the usual
  fate of a logo kept in two places. If the icon changes, paste the new
  paths in here and the wordmark follows; the translate is the only thing
  that belongs to this file.

  The letters are filled rather than stroked. A monoline C beside a solid
  band reads as two logos sharing a line. The C's curve is 14 units
  against the F's 13 stem because equal numbers look unequal: a curve has
  to be a shade heavier than a straight to match it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="234dp" android:height="56dp"
    android:viewportWidth="234" android:viewportHeight="56">

    <path android:pathData="M54.2,18 A28,28 0 1 0 54.2,38 L37.8,38 A14,14 0 1 1 37.8,18 Z">
